                        <field name="dc_description">Printed by Alex. Thom & Co., 87, 88, & 89, Abbey-Street, the Queen's Printing Office. -- Includes bibliographical references. -- Includes appendix. -- Cover title. -- "Appendix. ... chief parts of Mr. Butler's report to the late Under-Secretary [Thomas Henry Burke] ... Mallow, April 15th, 1882": p.[38]-40; "Mr. Butler" is almost certainly the "resident magistrate at Mallow". -- Recommends, inter alia, establishing a closer connection between the Magistracy and the Constabulary, with the District Inspector of the Royal Irish Constabulary reporting through the Resident Magistrate; probably addressed to the Secretary of State for Ireland or the Under-Secretary. </field>
